      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this doesn\u0027t quite work because `Simplify` has a bug. `Simplify` has an early inexpensive check to see if the path is convex. If it is then there isn\u0027t any need to simplify and the path can just be returned as-is. However, `SkPath::computeConvexity` has a special case and extra code to ensure that a path with no area made up of verbs that return to the starting point the way it came is considered \"convex\". This means that `Simplify` does not simplify these zero area paths to nothing as expected. What `Simplify` wants is a \"strictly convex\" check where when the `cross \u003d\u003d 0` and `dot \u003c 0` (going directly backwards) doesn\u0027t count as convex.",
      "revId": "47253cda733a6d93efb166855c72e76f8f4a9b1a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
