      "side": 1,
      "message": "The actual behavior of `SkPath::computeConvexity` is a bit more subtle at the moment than what I described. For example the `Convexicator::BySign` call is not just an accelerator, it protects the following checks from paths with more than three points (or more than two lines) from backward segments changing direction (and classifying some concave paths as convex).\n\nAfter considering many options, the fix may be to introduce  a `SkPath::isConvexDoubledBack()` or some such thing so that `Simplify` can change its early out convexity predicate to something like `path.isConvex() \u0026\u0026 !path.isConvexDoubledBack() \u0026\u0026 !path.isEmpty()`.",
